#---
# purpose: "a field read on a value the compiler knows is no map still compiles, and raises BadMapError when it runs, as in Elixir"
# oracle: self
# oracle.stamp: 2283420798522acb
#---
#
# The binary is known at the read, so the read can never find a map. That is
# no compile error: the read takes its miss arm and raises when it is reached.
defmodule Main do
  def main() do
    v = "bin"
    v.a
  rescue
    e in BadMapError -> IO.puts(Exception.message(e))
  end
end

Main.main()
